{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For a keeping throughout your generations.</b> Three keepings are stated here, as it is written <b>before YHWH, for a keeping throughout your generations</b>, and it is written <b>before the testimony, for a keeping</b>, <b>for a keeping throughout your generations, that they may see the bread</b> — this is the wilderness generation; 'before YHWH, for a keeping' — that is, in the land of Israel at the end of days, for the jar of the manna and the rod of Aharon, its almonds and blossoms, and the ark and its poles and all the work of the Tabernacle were hidden away in the tunnels beneath the Sanctuary. And who hid them away? King Yoshiyahu hid them away at the time when Hilkiyahu the priest found the scroll of the Torah open in the Sanctuary. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in tractate Horayot, chapter 'Kohen Meshuḥa': from the time the ark was hidden away, hidden away with it were the jar of the manna, the flask of the anointing oil, and the rod of Aharon, its almonds and blossoms, and the chest that the Philistines sent as a gift to the God of Israel, as it is said (I Samuel 6:8): ״ואת כלי הזהב אשר השיבותם לו אשם תשימו בארגז מצדו״. And who hid them away? Yoshiyahu king of Judah, who saw written in the Torah (Deuteronomy 28:36): ״יולך ה' אותך ואת מלכך״, etc. — he commanded and hid them away, as it is said (II Chronicles 35:3): ״ויאמר ללוים לכל ישראל המלמדים קדש לה׳ תנו את ארון הקדש בבית אשר בנה שלמה בן דוד מלך ישראל״. And R. Elazar said: it is derived 'generations' 'generations,' it is derived 'keeping' 'keeping': it is written concerning the rod of Aharon (Numbers 17:25): ״השב את מטה אהרן לפני העדות למשמרת לאות לבני מרי״, and it is written here: למשמרת לדורותיכם, and it is written: לפני העדות למשמרת — to teach you that they were hidden away in one place."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "Rabbeinu Bahya cites the chapter name as 'כהן משוח' but the standard chapter heading in tractate Horayot is 'משוח מלחמה'; rendered as printed. The Chronicles verse is cited as דברי הימים ב ל״ה:ג׳ and rendered from the full Hebrew verse as Rabbeinu Bahya quotes it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:20.121040971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}